mode: "100644"
text: "# Podcast → social 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile (tools/pricing move). Re-verify quarterly at each tool's site.*\n\n## The POV: a podcast is long-form; social is short, visual, sound-off\nThe skill isn't \"make a podcast\" — it's the **audio→social pipeline:** turn the best **30–90 second** moments\ninto **branded, captioned** clips/audiograms that **drive people back to the full episode.** A 60-min episode\nis the whole pizza; a clip is one irresistible slice. **55% of Americans listen to podcasts monthly** (record\nhigh, Edison 2025); **85% watch social video sound-off** → **captions are non-optional.**\n\n## The top-1% lever: select by retention, not vibes\nPull clips from **listener-retention spikes** — Spotify for Podcasters / Apple / **YouTube Studio** show where\npeople **replayed/rewatched** (a spike = a moment that landed). Map spikes → timestamps → clips. **AI virality\nscores are a starting point, not the decider.** And don't re-listen: the **timestamped transcript is your\nproduction map.**\n\n## Two formats (+ a third)\n- **Video-podcast clip** (if you recorded video) — **9:16 vertical**, auto-reframe to the **active speaker**,\n  burned-in captions. 30–90s.\n- **Audiogram** (audio-only) — **cover art/background + animated waveform** (bars/circles/lines/blobs) +\n  **captions + title.** Makes audio visual + sound-off-accessible; beats a static image — but **real video\n  clips outperform audiograms** (2025–26 practitioner consensus; attribute), so if video exists, clip it, and\n  consider recording video going forward. An audio-only audiogram must be **caption-first**: the words carry\n  it; the waveform is support, not the star.\n- **Quote card** — a single strong line as a graphic (→ `design-and-templates`).\n\n## The pipeline\n```\nrecord -> transcribe (Descript/Castmagic) -> timestamp standout moments (claims/data/reactions/stories; + retention spikes)\n-> generate 5-8 clips/audiograms -> add hook + captions + branding -> strategic CTA -> publish across platforms on a cadence\n```\nOpusClip generates ~12–24 clips from a 60-min episode; you keep the best **5–8.** Processing ~10–20 min/hour.\n\n## Tools (verify-quarterly)\n- **Clip makers:** **Opus Clip** (repurposing engine; AI Virality Score; active-speaker reframe; free ~60–90\n  min watermarked, Pro 300+ min/no watermark/4K; **struggles with non-talking-head / B-roll / screen-share**;\n  little creative control — add the hook/overlay elsewhere), **Choppity** (best conversational-podcast accuracy\n  2026), **Descript** (text-based **editor** + filler-word removal + publishes to Spotify/Apple/YouTube — the\n  editor, not a clip engine), **Kapwing** (best free; audiogram support; 100+ languages), Vizard/Vidyo.ai/\n  Submagic.\n- **Audiogram makers:** **Headliner** (the classic audiogram builder — waveform styles, artwork, captions,\n  templates, multi-aspect, RSS monitoring, Eddy AI; free 5 unwatermarked/mo, ~$7.99 Basic, ~$19.99 Pro),\n  **Podsqueeze**, Opus.pro audiogram tool.\n- **Written repurposing:** **Castmagic** (audio → show notes/blog/captions/quotes). **Distribution:**\n  Repurpose.io. **Design:** Canva (→ `design-and-templates`). **Video-clip caption burn-in:** →\n  `captions-and-clipping` / `clipping.md`.\n\n## Best practice\nCaptions on **every** clip; **hook in the first 3s**; **strategic CTA** (a *reason* to watch the full ep — a\nteaser/cliffhanger — not \"check out the full episode\"); unique/relatable/personal-experience snippets get\nshared most; consistent branding (logo/colors/templates); SEO keywords in description/tags. **Cadence\nexample:** episode Mon → clip Tue → blog Wed → quote graphic Thu → newsletter Fri → carousel next Mon (one\nepisode → a week+ of content, <2 hrs overhead).\n"
